[
  {
    "sha": "86853050d2115e1779c3eec26c8f1852a1dcf54b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDg2ODUzMDUwZDIxMTVlMTc3OWMzZWVjMjZjOGYxODUyYTFkY2Y1NGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T05:42:16Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T05:42:16Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(catalog): add the turning case cone-thread - a cone with a threaded end\n\nThe case examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread turns a 30 mm bar to a\n20 mm to 10 mm cone with a neck and an M10x1.5 thread, on the built-in\n2-axis lathe with the Fanuc lathe post: face, rough profile, finish\nprofile, neck groove, thread (G32 passes), part-off.\n\nThe profile operations cut to a turned-blank model and the neck, thread\nand part-off cut to the finished model, because Profile Finish reads the\nthread valleys and the neck step as rest (issue 2880). The thread posts\nas G32 passes, because a G76 cycle would start inside the part (issues\n2878 and 2879). The shoulder is sharp, because a fillet sends the\nprofile rides far out of the bar (issue 2881).\n\nPinned by example_catalog::turning_cone_thread_case_posts_the_taper_and_the_thread\nand the two suite tests that iterate all catalog cases.\n\nFixes #2394\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
